 "headlines": [
  "<b>AVGO</b> is the one to watch. It's inside a flip zone that has been moving ($308\u2013345), under its largest $315 level (+0.3K). There's almost no support below it, and none at all around $300. It's also the most negative board (\u221241.7K into opex), so swings are likely to be big.",
  "<b>NVDA</b> has the most positioning into opex (+166K), centred on $164\u2013170. It's also sitting on its $137\u2013166 flip zone.",
  "<b>GOOGL</b> is on its $277\u2013292 flip zone but net negative into opex (\u22126.8K), so swings are likely to be bigger. <b>TSLA</b> faces resistance at $390\u2013400 (and it's sitting on its $377\u2013394 flip zone), <b>AAPL</b> at $360 (and it's sitting on its $348 flip), and <b>AMZN</b> at $257.5\u2013260 (and it's sitting on its $248\u2013258 flip zone).",
  "Looking to the 1/15 opex, <b>AAPL</b> has the most positioning (+330K); <b>AVGO</b> stays net negative into both opex dates; <b>GOOGL</b> and <b>TSM</b> flip from negative this month to positive; <b>NVDA</b> flips from positive this month to negative.",
  "<b>TSM</b> is the next-weakest board, at only \u221236.1K into opex. It's inside its $327\u2013368 flip zone, and TradeEcho rates it 3/5."
 ],
